Verdict legend:
- 'W!' on Δneg = Weyl violation (neg increased as α grew).
- 'W!' on Δnz  = (neg+zero) violation.
- For uniform α·I: λ_i(A+αI) = λ_i(A)+α, so neg(α) must be
non-increasing. Any Weyl violation = pivot-selection jitter
that misclassifies an eigenvalue across the zero line.
- For x-block-only α·diag(1_x): the additive perturbation is
PSD on the x-block, so eigenvalues only move 'up' — neg
must still be non-increasing as α → ∞.
- rel_resid = ||A_shifted x - b|| / ||b|| with random b. If
small (≲ 1e-6) at a Weyl-violation α, the L·D·L^T factor is
correct and only the inertia counter is buggy. If large,
the factor itself is wrong.
